{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>They have dealt corruptly with Him, not His children, their blemish</b> — a blemish (מוּם) is called corruption (שְׁחָתָה), as it is written (Leviticus 22:25) \"because their corruption is in them, a blemish is in them,\" and likewise \"and sacrifices a corrupt thing to YHWH\" (Malachi 1:14). He says: the blemish of Israel — they have dealt corruptly with the Rock of His people and His inheritance. And He calls them <b>not His children</b>, in contrast to when He calls them \"My children\" in a time of favor. And He says that they are \"a twisted and perverse generation,\" for twistedness (עִקְּשׁוּת) is the opposite of uprightness (יֹשֶׁר), as in what is written (Micah 3:9) \"and they twist all that is straight,\" and perverse (פְּתַלְתֹּל) is the opposite of just (צַדִּיק). And since He is just and upright and the people are the opposite of this, they are not His children; rather, they are corrupters to Him. The versification of the verse is: \"They have dealt corruptly to Him — their blemish — those who are not His children, a twisted and perverse generation.\" Now the sense is that the deficiency in their virtue does not result from the Rock's action, for He is perfect and no deficiency will ever occur in Him; rather, their blemish is what corrupts them before their Father. And the sense of <b>not His children</b> is like \"and I will say to 'not-My-people': You are My people\" (Hosea 2:25), and likewise \"they have provoked Me with a no-god\" (Deuteronomy 32:21) — with that which is not a god — and \"they have sworn by those who are not gods\" (Jeremiah 5:7). Alternatively, he may say: \"they dealt corruptly to Him — their blemish\" — in that they are not His children, for they are a twisted and perverse generation, the opposite of Him:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:57:57.110941573Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}